# Type chips / small labels — uppercase

Any **project type**, **article type**, or other small UI label uses `text-transform: uppercase` (FK Grotesk Mono Medium / `--font-label`).

On Projects + Insights surfaces, type labels are **plain text** (no chip fill): Mono Medium, shared `--type-chip-font`, gray ink, **all caps**. Title/description in those metas are white. See `mobile-meta-chip-right.mdc`.

Applies to:

- `.insight-chip` / `.insight-chip--on-media`
- `.project-type-chip` / `.project-type-chip--on-media`
- `.project-case-demo__tag`
- Filter involvement pills (`.project-involvement__pill`)
- Any future type label on covers or cards

# Insight label tokens (size / tracking for non-chip microcopy)

Shared tokens on `.insights-page` and `.insight-detail` for date / eyebrows / filter microcopy:

- `--insight-label-tracking: 0.08em`
- `--insight-label-size: clamp(0.625rem, 0.58rem + 0.2vw, 0.75rem)`
- `--insight-meta-gap: 1.75rem`

Do not invent a different letter-spacing or font-size for those micro-labels on one Insights surface and another.
